==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|īren}}, {{l|ang|īsen}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*īsarną}}, probably from {{der|ang|cel-pro|*īsarnom}}, derived from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*h₁ésh₂r̥||blood}}. Cognates include {{cog|ofs|īsern}} ({{cog|fy|izer}}), {{cog|osx|īsarn}} ({{cog|nds|Iesen}}), {{cog|odt|*īsarn}} ({{cog|nl|ijzer}}), {{cog|goh|īsarn}} ({{cog|de|Eisen}}), {{cog|non|járn}} ({{cog|sv|järn}}), {{cog|got|𐌴𐌹𐍃𐌰𐍂𐌽}}, {{cog|sga|īärn}} ({{cog|ga|iarann}}, {{cog|cy|haearn}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈiːsern/|[ˈiːzerˠn]}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n|head=īsern|īsern}}

# the metal [[iron]]
# an instrument or tool made from iron, especially an iron [[sword]]
# an iron [[shackle]] or [[fetter]]

